Bundled binaries
----------------
Every installer ships `resources/omp` (macOS arm64), `resources/omp.x64`
(macOS Intel), `resources/omp.exe` (Windows x64) or the Linux equivalent: a
**compiled binary of upstream oh-my-pi's coding agent**, built unmodified from
the monorepo commit recorded in `sidecar-source.json`. WISA does not patch the
agent. Those binaries are upstream's work under the MIT License above, and they
are never committed to this repository — they are build artifacts produced by
`bun run build:omp*`.

What WISA adds
--------------
- Product name, window titles, tray labels, installer artifact names.
- Vietnamese localization of the interface (upstream ships English, Chinese,
  Russian and Thai).
- A pre-seeded `wisa` provider pointing at https://api.askwisa.com/v1, so one
  WISA API key reaches every model the gateway serves. Any other provider the
  upstream agent supports still works.
- Release metadata pointing at this repository.

Bundled and downloaded components
---------------------------------
Piper (https://github.com/rhasspy/piper, MIT) and the Vietnamese voice model
vi_VN-vais1000-medium (CC BY 4.0, from rhasspy/piper-voices) are downloaded on
first use, not shipped in the installer. Neither is committed to this
repository; both are verified against a pinned SHA-256 before use.

